---
import distribution from '../lib/get-ready-package.json';
import { Download, Code, Terminal } from '@lucide/astro';
const install='npm install --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund ./get-ready-core.tgz';
---
<div class="core-download" aria-labelledby="core-download-title">
 <div class="download-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">For agents, developers and platform teams</p><h3 id="core-download-title">Use the engine in your own tool.</h3></div><span class="small">v{distribution.version} · MIT · Node 22</span></div>
 <p>Download the same library and command used by Composer. Keep your own interface, workspace and credentials. The archive has no runtime package dependencies or install scripts.</p>
 <div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href={distribution.url} download="get-ready-core.tgz"><Download size={18} aria-hidden="true"/>Download Get Ready</a><a href="/downloads/get-ready-core.json" download="get-ready-core.json">Source & checksum manifest</a></div>
 <p class="small">{Math.ceil(distribution.bytes/1024)} KB · {distribution.developmentSnapshot?'Development snapshot':'Release source'} <a href={`https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/tree/${distribution.source}/lib/get-ready`}><code>{distribution.source.slice(0,12)}</code></a>. Review the source and bundled README before running it. The manifest checks a matching download; it is not an independent signature.</p>
 <details><summary><Terminal size={17} aria-hidden="true"/>Install the downloaded archive</summary><p>Check the archive’s SHA-256 against the manifest, then install it in the local project you chose for this integration.</p><pre><code>{install}{'\n'}./node_modules/.bin/get-ready --help{'\n'}./node_modules/.bin/get-ready --workspace /absolute/authorised/workspace --report</code></pre><p>The last command checks that workspace and saves private progress there. An incomplete setup returns a report with the next action. Setup operations require a separate explicit request. This archive is served here; it has not been published to the npm registry.</p><p class="small">SHA-256 <code class="checksum">{distribution.sha256}</code></p></details>
 <details><summary><Code size={17} aria-hidden="true"/>Library, API and MCP</summary><p>Import <code>runLocalReadiness</code>, <code>referenceTarget</code> and <code>readinessReport</code> from <code>@loftwah/get-ready</code>. The bundled README has a working integration example. Session and adapter exports use the same engine; report and address-preference modules have separate exports.</p><p>The optional <a href="#local-get-ready-mcp">local MCP adapter</a> stays in the source repository with its SDK dependencies. It is not in this archive. A hosted API is still unexposed.</p></details>
</div>
<style>
.core-download{border-block:1px solid var(--color-border);padding:28px 0;margin:28px 0}.download-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;align-items:baseline}.download-heading h3{font-size:1.5rem;margin:8px 0 16px}.eyebrow{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-accent);margin:0}.core-download details{margin-top:16px}.core-download summary{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;cursor:pointer;padding:10px 0;min-height:44px;font-weight:500}.core-download summary::before{content:'+';font:20px/1 system-ui}.core-download details[open] summary::before{content:'−'}.core-download summary svg{flex-shrink:0}.checksum{overflow-wrap:anywhere;word-break:break-all}.core-download pre{max-width:100%;overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:18px;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:6px}.core-download p{max-width:76ch}@media(max-width:600px){.download-heading{flex-direction:column;gap:0}.download-heading h3{margin-bottom:10px}.download-heading>.small{margin-bottom:12px}.core-download{padding:24px 0}}
</style>
